        <body>
            <div xml:id="d681-a3">

                <pb facs="0792" n="707" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg707"/>

                <head>No. 5</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">British
                            Legation</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-08-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 9,
                    1919</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">sir p. cox to his highness
                        vossug-ed-dowleh</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Highness</hi>, With reference to the second
                    desideratum indicated in my previous letter of to-day’s date, it is understood
                    and agreed between the two Governments reciprocally that, on the one hand His
                    Majesty’s Government will not claim from the Government of His Majesty the Shah
                    the cost of the maintenance of British troops which His Majesty’s Government
                    were obliged to send to Persia owing to Persia’s want of power to defend her
                    neutrality, and that on the other hand the Persian Government will not claim
                    from the British Government an indemnity for any damage which may have been
                    caused by the said troops during their presence in Persian territory.</p>
                <p>It is to be understood, however, that this agreement of the two parties does not
                    in any way affect the claims of individuals and private institutions, which will
                    be dealt with independently.</p>
                <p>A note from your Highness informing me that you accept this position on behalf of
                    the Persian Government will suffice to record the agreement of the two
                    Governments on this subject.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>(Signed) <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. Z.
                    Cox</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
